<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hikayat Aceh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hikayat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> is a Malay court chronicle of the Aceh Sultanate, written in the 17th century in praise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iskandar-muda">Iskandar Muda</a>. It tells of his ancestry, birth and youth in a style influenced by Persian royal biographies, and survives only incompletely. It is a major source for the history and court culture of Aceh at the height of its power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hikayat-aceh.jpg" alt="Hikayat Aceh" width="320" height="524" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hikayat_Aceh_Or._1954_(Leiden).pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
